<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mount Merapi</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mount Merapi is an active volcano in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, north of Yogyakarta, and one of the most active in the world. Its ash made the surrounding plains fertile and supported early Javanese kingdoms such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medang-kingdom">Medang</a>, whose court moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-java">East Java</a> in 929, possibly after eruptions. Major eruptions in modern times, including those of 1930 and 2010, have killed hundreds of people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mount-merapi.jpg" alt="Mount Merapi" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fahmi Widayat · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pendidikan_Karakter_Dan_Nasionalisme.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
